Id: sysd007i
Severity: INFO
Category: services
Check: check_units
References: systemd.unit(5)
Controls: CIS 4.1; NIST CM-5, CM-6; ISO 8.9; CE Secure configuration

Some enabled systemd services are not shipped by a package: their
unit files are in /etc/systemd/system, written by hand or by a
program's installer, or in /run/systemd/system, generated at boot
(netplan writes some there). The detail lists them. They are worth
knowing about, since no package update fixes them and no package
database vouches for them: check what each runs, with 'systemctl cat
NAME'. This is informational.
